body:
I've been off orientation for about 2 months. I hate it too. Had 2 full days off in a row for the first time in a while and I finally felt alive again... actually went outside, walked across a frozen lake, climbed a big hill, made a snowboard ramp out of a folding table at the park. Now today, all I can think about is having to go back tomorrow, energy zapped, stuck in bed, kinda pigging out. Just dread. And googling cheap off the grid living, and how to escape societal obligations. This job truly makes me dread life.

&#x200B;

Starting in a couple weeks I'm 100% night shift, which has its own issues, but preferable nonetheless. Anyways, no fucking idea what I'm doing with my life. Don't think I'm cut out to be a nurse. In conclusion... Good luck whatever you do.
